/*
Problem: Minimum Generations
Platform: LeetCode (LC 3923)
Topic: Simulation / Hashing / Geometry

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

Initially we are given some 3D points.

In one generation:

Take every pair of EXISTING points.

Generate their midpoint.

If the midpoint is new,
add it to the set of points.

Repeat until:

• target is generated
or
• no new point can be generated.

---------------------------------------------------------

Key Observation:

Points generated in previous generations
can also participate in generating
future midpoints.

Therefore we maintain one growing list:

allpts

instead of using only the original points.

---------------------------------------------------------

Data Structures:

1. unordered_set

Stores every generated point.

Allows O(1) lookup.

--------------------------------

2. vector allpts

Stores all available points.

Original + newly generated.

--------------------------------

3. vector newpts

Stores only the points created
during the current generation.

They are appended after the generation
finishes.

---------------------------------------------------------

Hash Function:

unordered_set cannot directly store
vector<int>.

So we define a custom hash.

For point

(x,y,z)

Hash:

x * 1000000

+

y * 1000

+

z

---------------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

Step 1

If target already exists

Return 0.

--------------------------------

Step 2

Insert all initial points into

unordered_set

and

allpts.

--------------------------------

Step 3

Repeat:

generation++

--------------------------------

For every pair:

(i, j)

Compute midpoint.

mid.x = (x1+x2)/2

mid.y = (y1+y2)/2

mid.z = (z1+z2)/2

--------------------------------

If midpoint is new:

If midpoint == target

Return current generation.

Otherwise:

Insert into

set

and

newpts.

--------------------------------

After checking all pairs:

If no new point was created

Return -1.

Otherwise append every point
from newpts into allpts.

Repeat.

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

Initial:

(0,0,0)

(2,2,2)

Target:

(1,1,1)

--------------------------------

Generation 1

Midpoint:

(1,1,1)

Target found.

Answer = 1

---------------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The set guarantees:

No duplicate point is processed twice.

The growing list guarantees:

Newly generated points can generate
future points.

Simulation continues until either:

Target appears

or

No further progress is possible.

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

Suppose total generated points = N

Every generation compares pairs.

Worst case:

O(N²)

---------------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity:

O(N)

For storing generated points.

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:

    // Custom hash for vector<int>
    struct hashVec {
        int operator()(const vector<int>& v) const {
            return v[0] * 1000000 +
                   v[1] * 1000 +
                   v[2];
        }
    };

    int minGenerations(vector<vector<int>>& points,
                       vector<int>& target) {

        // Target already exists
        for (auto &p : points) {
            if (p == target)
                return 0;
        }

        unordered_set<vector<int>, hashVec> st;

        // Stores every point generated so far
        vector<vector<int>> allpts;

        for (auto &p : points) {
            st.insert(p);
            allpts.push_back(p);
        }

        int generation = 0;

        while (true) {

            generation++;

            vector<vector<int>> newpts;

            int n = allpts.size();

            // Generate midpoints
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

                for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {

                    if (allpts[i] == allpts[j])
                        continue;

                    vector<int> mid(3);

                    mid[0] = (allpts[i][0] + allpts[j][0]) / 2;
                    mid[1] = (allpts[i][1] + allpts[j][1]) / 2;
                    mid[2] = (allpts[i][2] + allpts[j][2]) / 2;

                    // New point discovered
                    if (st.find(mid) == st.end()) {

                        if (mid == target)
                            return generation;

                        st.insert(mid);
                        newpts.push_back(mid);
                    }
                }
            }

            // No new point generated
            if (newpts.empty())
                return -1;

            // Add newly generated points
            for (auto &p : newpts)
                allpts.push_back(p);
        }
    }
};
